review-verdict-rev7.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev8.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-37e5e2.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-b4446d.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-rev7.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-cr10.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-cr9.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-rev4.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-rework.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-v060.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev10.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev2.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev3.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev4.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev6.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev7.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev8.md\\nTASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev9.md\\n===\\nRework the name-query candidate of TASK-260830-21gygk after the CR10 independent changes-requested verdict by RUN-260916-64d466 (Astra low). Read TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev10.md and materialize TASK-260830-21gygk_review-evidence-rev10.tar.gz (TestReview10ReferencedCheckpointAdmission with its 12 negatives and 4 controls, raw logs). Candidate tree 106f5e99000827f20cfae6780c6f93eb4321c505 on the refreshed base 9ff7d2c1d4d391dbc58d40b812757052d324a775 in the managed Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree (branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns; checkpoints 7189c41 and 1f34c0c) — continue from the uncommitted CR10 candidate; preserve checkpointed predecessors and all foreign changes; no manual commits, no direct .task-board edits, no self-acceptance. Superseded briefs (republish-rev10, rework-rev9 and earlier) are context only; this brief governs.\\n\\nCR10 closed CR9 P1-A/P1-B and the P2 accounting, and opened the fifth member of the C6 family: referencedCheckpointProfile (internal/sessquery/lease.go around 892-918) treats an entry of map[string]validatedCheckpoint as admitted authority after only session equality and event-head membership; the map is canonically parsed, not semantically admitted, so a referenced resume checkpoint with the wrong creator/holder, the wrong persistence variant for the Session Record kind, or a fencing token without an admitted owning lease at that epoch is consumed as authority (12 of 12 negatives admitted through BuildPlan, fresh Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList; old plans still refuse stale correctly). SPEC 5.4 binds lease_id to the owning lease fencing token, created_by_host_id to its holder and the persistence variant to the Session Record kind; SPEC 5.2/5.4 require the referenced checkpoint's authority, not a canonical record with known event IDs.\\n\\nClose the class, not the arm. First extend the instrument: add to the relation census a record-consumption table — every record the shared owner consumes (Session Record, winner checkpoint, necessary-ancestor checkpoint, REFERENCED resume checkpoint, lease records, profile.changed and other events) with the semantic admission owner that must admit it before it is used (checkWinnerCheckpoint / checkCheckpointBinding / lease admission / creator-holder / Session.kind variant), the call site, the positive control, the negatives (wrong creator, wrong variant, wrong lease/fencing token, missing, read-failed) and the narrowing plant; then make the code match it: route the referenced checkpoint through the SAME semantic admission owner the winner and necessary-ancestor checkpoints use (with the winning ancestry and Session.kind inputs it needs — these are already supplied to the shared reader; do not build storage, transport, publication or materialization), keep historical/branching/lagging references admitted, keep missing versus read-failed distinct (observation_unavailable vs integrity_failure as before), and add a gate that fails if any consumed record reaches the profile derivation without passing its admission owner (for example a census test over the call graph, or an admitted-record type that only the admission owner can construct and that the derivation requires). Port TestReview10ReferencedCheckpointAdmission RED first, keep its 12 negatives and 4 controls across direct/task_board and winner/necessary-ancestor, add old-plan variants, and add narrowing plants for the referenced-admission path whose kills are behavioral admission failures.\\n\\nKeep everything CR10 established: TestReview9* and TestRev10* green, the referenced-closure resume derivation, the fork arm, the accounting (60 unique N/B plants, 43 semantic-admission and 17 precision, applied harmless SURVIVED control, NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE outside the numerator) extended honestly with the new plants and per-plant raw logs, exits from subprocess return codes. Retain the closed CR7/CR8 findings and the accepted CLI/publication/storage/transport/effects boundary; 8-row AC denominator, 0 of 8 CLI rows (stated bound). Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the affected package tests while iterating and the full configured validation once before handoff. Budget: the run has 4 hours and the runtime's 26-command validation suite runs after your handoff — hand off no later than 3 hours in. Leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED. Attach TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev11.md, TASK-260830-21gygk_conformance-matrix-rev11.md, TASK-260830-21gygk_relation-census-rev11.md (with the record-consumption table) and TASK-260830-21gygk_producer-evidence-rev11.tar.gz, then hand off through task-board and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6324,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1581,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
