nged paths). This is the rework after the CR9 changes-requested verdict (TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev9.md, evidence tar rev9); read that verdict, the producer outcome TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev10.md (the rework was produced by RUN-260916-dea59a, which the launcher killed at its 4h budget during CR construction; RUN-260916-2ef543 only refreshed the base and republished the identical candidate — its appended Republish section and the source manifest in the evidence tarball prove the bytes are the finished rev10 state), the conformance matrix rev10, the relation census TASK-260830-21gygk_relation-census-rev10.md, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. Superseded briefs (reviewer-cr9 and earlier) are historical; this brief governs.\\n\\nThe CR7/CR8/CR9 verdicts form one family: canonical shape or outer-walk position accepted in place of cross-record authority for the profile pair. Review the census first: it must enumerate every (event kind x relationship) row of SPEC 5.2's pair rule with 2.4/5.4 — provider.launched first/later, task_board.launched first/later, session.resumed, fork.created — each with its authority input (Session Record; effective profile at the REFERENCED checkpoint's own event-head closure resolved through checkpoint_id and the admitted Checkpoint Record), owner arm, positive control, negatives (missing/read-failed/contradictory/non-newest/later-local-only/losing-lease/wrong-session) and narrowing plant. An undriven row that is not a named caller bound with its owning clause is a finding. Then verify the shared owner (checkCheckpointProfileAuthority / checkClosureProfilePairs / checkProfilePairSource) against the census: rerun TestReview9ForkLocalProfile and TestReview9ResumeReferencedCheckpoint on the exact candidate (both negatives must now refuse with the pinned class, controls pass), and probe at least one census row the producer did not witness through BuildPlan, fresh and old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList across direct/task_board and winner/necessary-ancestor. Confirm the resume expectation is derived from the referenced checkpoint closure, not from the outer walk, and that historical/branching/lagging controls still admit.\\n\\nP2 accounting: the manifests must report the real plant inventory (56 unique N/B plants at CR9: 39 semantic-admission, 17 label/class/output-precision) plus the new plants, with per-plant raw logs, exits from subprocess return codes, the harmless SURVIVED control applied through the same harness, and NOT_APPLIED / COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE reported outside the numerator; classify every new kill as semantic admission, precision, or fixture failure and reject any blanket narrowing total.\\n\\nRetain closed findings unless new evidence contradicts them: CR7 heads and old-plan substitution; CR8 missing-source refusals and real profile changes; direct/task_board persistence variants; necessary ancestry/creator; canonical lease identity; lagging copies; parked required source; seven capabilities; predecessor/reducer/enums/creation crashes. Re-derive the 8-row AC accounting and the public-caller bounds from source; the CLI rows remain a stated bound.\\n\\nMethod: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; reuse earlier evidence only with exact provenance. Attach TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev10.md and TASK-260830-21gygk_review-evidence-rev10.tar.gz, complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-21gygk, revision=10, evidence=TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev10.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2 classes and repeat-of named. Model: codex gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4489,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1123,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}