{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf23","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0abc2-42f2-7250-afbe-0f50f97f1bdf"},"sequence":1516,"recorded_at":1780531400003027,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0abca-6fb5-7022-978e-3dc4eebed21a"},"task_id":"01a0abca-6fb5-7022-978e-3dc4eebed21a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0abca-6fb5-7022-978e-3dc4eebed21a","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/lease.go`.\n(509 line(s) above)\n510|func (reader *Reader) checkAncestorCheckpoints(chain []validatedLease, sessionKind string, repo *sessrepo.Repository) error {\n511|\tif len(chain) < 2 {\n512|\t\treturn nil\n513|\t}\n514|\tcheckpoints, err := reader.validatedCheckpointsByDigest()\n515|\tif err != nil {\n516|\t\treturn err\n517|\t}\n518|\tfor index := 1; index < len(chain); index++ {\n519|\t\tcurrent := chain[index]\n520|\t\tif current.Epoch == 1 {\n521|\t\t\tif !current.HasCheckpoint {\n522|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n523|\t\t\t}\n524|\t\t\tif err := checkCheckpointBinding(current, current, checkpoints, sessionKind, repo); err != nil {\n525|\t\t\t\treturn err\n526|\t\t\t}\n527|\t\t\tcontinue\n528|\t\t}\n529|\t\tif !current.HasCheckpoint {\n530|\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: validated checkpoint for session %s lease %s cannot be established\", ErrObservationUnavailable, current.SessionID, current.LeaseID)\n531|\t\t}\n532|\t\tif index+1 >= len(chain) {\n533|\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: predecessor lease record for session %s cannot be established\", ErrObservationUnavailable, current.SessionID)\n534|\t\t}\n535|\t\tif err := checkCheckpointBinding(current, chain[index+1], checkpoints, sessionKind, repo); err != nil {\n536|\t\t\treturn err\n537|\t\t}\n538|\t}\n539|\treturn nil\n540|}\n541|\n542|// checkCheckpointBinding resolves one lease's checkpoint reference\n543|// against the admitted Checkpoint Records and validates its Section\n544|// 5.3 session and predecessor-lease binding with its Section 5.4\n545|// holder binding: the checkpoint must name this session and the\n546|// owning lease, and its creator must be that lease's holder. The\n547|// admitted checkpoint must also resolve its event-head closure in\n548|// the winning source chain (repo); see checkCheckpointEventHeads.\n549|// The same closure must then admit its Section 2.4 profile\n550|// authority; see checkCheckpointProfileAuthority.\n551|func checkCheckpointBinding(current, owner validatedLease, checkpoints map[string]validatedCheckpoint, sessionKind string, repo *sessrepo.Repository) error {\n552|\tcheckpoint, ok := checkpoints[current.Checkpoint]\n553|\tif !ok {\n554|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: validated checkpoint %s for session %s cannot be established\", ErrObservationUnavailable, current.Checkpoint, current.SessionID)\n555|\t}\n556|\tif checkpoint.SessionID != current.SessionID {\n557|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: validated checkpoint %s carries session %s, want %s\", ErrObservationUnavailable, current.Checkpoint, checkpoint.SessionID, current.SessionID)\n558|\t}\n559|\tif checkpoint.LeaseEpoch != owner.Epoch || checkpoint.LeaseID != owner.LeaseID {\n560|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: validated checkpoint %s is bound to lease %s at epoch %d, want lease %s at epoch %d\", ErrObservationUnavailable, current.Checkpoint, checkpoint.LeaseID, checkpoint.LeaseEpoch, owner.LeaseID, owner.Epoch)\n561|\t}\n562|\tif checkpoint.CreatorHostID != owner.HolderHostID {\n563|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: validated checkpoint %s is created by host %s, want owning lease holder %s\", ErrObservationUnavailable, current.Checkpoint, checkpoint.CreatorHostID, owner.HolderHostID)\n564|\t}\n565|\tif err := checkCheckpointPersistence(checkpoint, current.SessionID, sessionKind); err != nil {\n566|\t\treturn err\n567|\t}\n568|\tif err := checkCheckpointEventHeads(checkpoint, owner, repo); err != nil {\n569|\t\treturn err\n570|\t}\n571|\tif err := checkCheckpointProfileAuthority(checkpoint, repo, checkpoints); err != nil {\n572|\t\treturn err\n573|\t}\n574|\treturn nil\n575|}\n576|\n577|// checkCheckpointEventHeads resolves every event head of one admitted\n578|// Checkpoint Record against the winning source chain for its session\n579|// (Section 5.4 event-head closure). Each head must name a chained\n580|// event for the same session at or before the owning lease: a head\n581|// naming an absent event (including a cross-session digest, a\n582|// losing-lease preserved blob outside the authoritative chain, or a\n583|// synthetic placeholder) is incomplete authority\n584|// (observation_unavailable), and a head under a later lease (a\n585|// greater epoch, or the same epoch under a different fencing token)\n586|// is likewise incomplete authority because the checkpoint cannot fix\n587|// authority over events that postdate it. Historical heads stay\n588|// admissible and are never required to equal the current tail, so\n589|// valid branching and lagging copies are preserved. A failed chain\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
