 stay present so the static gate passes. |\n+| Referenced checkpoint variant | `TestReview10ReferencedCheckpointAdmission` (wrong_variant on direct/task_board winner and ancestor paths through all four entries), `TestRev11ReferencedCheckpointAdmissionRefusalClass/wrong_variant`, `TestRev11ReferencedCheckpointAdmissionOldPlan/wrong_variant` | N-referenced-variant admits exactly the idA wrong persistence variant on the referenced path; the wrong_variant negatives fail by admission while other variant mismatches still refuse observation_unavailable. The census call tokens stay present so the static gate passes. |\n+| Referenced checkpoint lease | `TestReview10ReferencedCheckpointAdmission` (wrong_lease on direct/task_board winner and ancestor paths through all four entries), `TestRev11ReferencedCheckpointAdmissionRefusalClass/wrong_lease`, `TestRev11ReferencedCheckpointAdmissionOldPlan/wrong_lease` | N-referenced-lease admits exactly the leaseCycleB fencing token past the owning-lease tuple match; the wrong_lease negatives fail by admission while other unowned tuples still refuse observation_unavailable. The census call tokens stay present so the static gate passes. |\n+| Record-consumption census gate | `TestRev11RecordConsumptionCensus` (resume path calls the shared referenced owner before deriving; the owner calls the shared persistence and head helpers) | The three N-referenced plants above are the token-preserving attacks: each keeps every searched-for call token while admitting one invalid member, so the static gate passes and the behavioral suites above must fail. The harness always executes the behavioral suites, never the static gate alone. |\n+| Historical closure fixation |\n","final_result":true}}}
