{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000deff","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0abc2-42f2-7250-afbe-0f50f97f1bdf"},"sequence":3546,"recorded_at":1780531400007087,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0abef-298a-7be2-a990-92a0ff6cab2c"},"task_id":"01a0abef-298a-7be2-a990-92a0ff6cab2c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0abef-298a-7be2-a990-92a0ff6cab2c","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/census-rev11-draft.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — Profile-pair relation census (rev10)\n2|\n3|Authority: AX v0.6.0 (`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`),\n4|pinned sentences:\n5|\n6|- SPEC 5.2: \"The profile and profile-source pair in every launch,\n7|  resume, and fork event MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile\n8|  at the referenced checkpoint or, for the first launch, the Session\n9|  Record and null; a non-null source MUST name the newest\n10|  authoritative `profile.changed` event in that event-head closure;\n11|  for `fork.created` the effective new-session authority is its newly\n12|  persisted Session Record so `profile_source_event_id` is null;\n13|  `source_profile_event_id` never participates\" in new-session\n14|  derivation.\n15|- SPEC 2.4: effective profile is the Session Record value followed by\n16|  the newest authoritative `profile.changed` event in lease/sequence\n17|  order; a checkpoint's event-head closure fixes both values; fork\n18|  creates a new authority boundary (new Session Record stores the\n19|  source-checkpoint effective profile, new-session source is null,\n20|  `source_profile_event_id` is provenance only).\n21|- SPEC 5.4: the transitive event-head closure fixes the effective\n22|  profile/source for its checkpoint; missing, losing-lease, or\n23|  non-newest references are `integrity_failure`; consumers MUST NOT\n24|  consult a later local-only event or fall back to creation.\n25|\n26|One row per (event kind x relationship). \"Entries\" = the four shared\n27|production entries `BuildPlan`, `Revalidate` (fresh + old-plan),\n28|`AuthoritativeStatus`, `AuthoritativeList`, all through\n29|`winningLeaseFor` -> `checkWinnerCheckpoint`/`checkCheckpointBinding`\n30|-> `checkCheckpointProfileAuthority` in\n31|`internal/sessquery/lease.go`. Every row is DRIVEN (named committed\n32|tests through the entries); nothing below is an undriven bound.\n33|Adjacent caller bounds are named with owning clauses at the end.\n34|\n35|## Census rows\n36|\n37|### R1 — provider.launched, first launch\n38|\n39|- Authority input: Session Record creation profile + null source. No\n40|  checkpoint input (5.2 \"for the first launch, the Session Record and\n41|  null\"; 13.1 step 5). Read via `repo.GetRecord` ->\n42|  `sessionCreationProfile`.\n43|- Production owner arm: `checkClosureProfilePairs`\n44|  provider/task_board.launched case, `firstLaunch` branch; presence\n45|  and value bound by `checkProfilePairSource`.\n46|- Positive control: `TestRev8CheckpointProfileAuthority`\n47|  (missing_source=false, direct/task_board x winner/ancestor);\n48|  `TestRev10ForkLocalProfile` good (launch after fork is still the\n49|  first launch); `TestRev10ResumeReferencedCheckpoint` good.\n50|- Negatives:\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
