{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e147","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0abc2-42f2-7250-afbe-0f50f97f1bdf"},"sequence":3838,"recorded_at":1780531400007671,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0abf7-1177-77e2-a30d-83d1ff7b2a47"},"task_id":"01a0abf7-1177-77e2-a30d-83d1ff7b2a47","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0abf7-1177-77e2-a30d-83d1ff7b2a47","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-102-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat > /tmp/gen_matrix_rev11.py <<'PY'\\nimport pathlib\\nrev10 = pathlib.Path('.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/matrix-rev11-draft.md').read_text()\\nrev11 = rev10.replace(\\n\\\"# TASK-260830-21gygk — Clause-to-owner conformance matrix (rev10 rework)\\\",\\n\\\"# TASK-260830-21gygk — Clause-to-owner conformance matrix (rev11 rework)\\\\n\\\\nRev11 change (CR10 P1, fifth C6 member): the R5 resume row now admits its\\\\nREFERENCED Checkpoint Record through the shared semantic owner\\\\n(`checkReferencedCheckpointBinding`) before deriving. The standalone\\\\ncensus file `TASK-260830-21gygk_relation-census-rev11.md` carries the same\\\\nsix pair rows plus the new K1-K7 record-consumption table; this matrix is\\\\nthat census in clause form. Battery: 63 unique N/B plants (60 N, 3 B):\\\\n46 semantic-admission, 17 precision.\\\"\\n)\\n# Update mutation accounting paragraph\\nold_acc = \\\"\\\"\\\"Mutation accounting (corrected per the CR9 verdict P2): the battery\\nholds 60 unique N/B plants (57 N, 3 B): 43 semantic-admission plants\\nwhose kill is a behavioral admission failure, and 17\\nlabel/class/output-precision plants (the 3 B output-order plants\\nplus 14 N plants). `N-checkpoint-heads` is a class/order precision\\nkill (weakened heads surface the wrong class through the profile\\nbackstop), not semantic admission. The three classifier controls\\n(harmless SURVIVED applied, NOT_APPLIED, COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE)\\nreport separately and never join the kill numerator.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nnew_acc = \\\"\\\"\\\"Mutation accounting (rev11, extending the corrected CR9 P2 base): the battery\\nholds 63 unique N/B plants (60 N, 3 B): 46 semantic-admission plants\\nwhose kill is a behavioral admission failure (43 retained + 3 new\\n`N-referenced-creator/variant/lease`), and 17\\nlabel/class/output-precision plants (the 3 B output-order plants\\nplus 14 N plants). `N-checkpoint-heads` is a class/order precision\\nkill (weakened heads surface the wrong class through the profile\\nbackstop), not semantic admission. The three classifier controls\\n(harmless SURVIVED applied via the same harness, NOT_APPLIED,\\nCOMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE) report separately and never join the kill\\nnumerator. New-plant kills are full-suite behavioral admission failures\\nwith per-plant raw logs and subprocess exits; the static census gate\\npasses for all three (token-preserving), so only the behavioral suites\\nfail.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nassert old_acc in rev11\\nrev11 = rev11.replace(old_acc, new_acc)\\n# Update C6b-R5 row: find the R5 table row (long). Replace shared admission cell to include referenced binding + new tests/plants.\\n# The R5 row starts with \\\"| C6b-R5 |\\\" and ends before \\\"| C6b-R6 |\\\". We'll replace the whole R5 row via splitting.\\nparts = rev11.split(\\\"| C6b-R5 |\\\")\\nassert len(parts)==2\\nhead, tail = parts\\nr5_and_rest = tail.split(\\\"| C6b-R6 |\\\")\\nassert len(r5_and_rest)==2\\nr5_old, rest = r5_and_rest\\n# Construct new R5 row (keep clause/relationship/canonical/boundary, update shared admission)\\n# Extract original R5 to preserve boundary? Simpler: replace shared admission phrases within r5_old.\\nr5_new = r5_old.replace(\\n\\\"OWNED (rev10 P1-B): `checkClosureProfilePairs` session.resumed case + `referencedCheckpointProfile` (`lease.go`): `checkpoint_id` -> admitted Checkpoint Record (`Reader.CheckpointRecords`, threaded through `checkWinnerCheckpoint`/`checkCheckpointBinding`) -> transitive closure over the winning-source index -> newest change. Source resolved against the REFERENCED closure. Missing/wrong-session/unresolvable references refuse `observation_unavailable`; contradictory pairs refuse `integrity_failure`. Tests: ported `TestReview9ResumeReferencedCheckpoint`, `TestRev10ResumeReferencedCheckpoint` (10 modes x direct/task_board x winner/ancestor with class pins), `TestRev10ResumeOldPlanSubstitution` (integrity), `TestRev10ResumeReferencedWithdrawal` (unavailable), updated `TestRev8ProfileResumePositiveControl` + `dangling_resume_source`. Plants: `N-profile-resume-missing` (admits exactly a missing-reference creation-pair resume; admission kill), `N-profile-resume-newest` (first referenced change wins; admission kill).\\\",\\n\\\"OWNED (rev10 P1-B + rev11 P1 referenced admission): `checkClosureProfilePairs` session.resumed case + `referencedCheckpointProfile` + `checkReferencedCheckpointBinding` (`lease.go`): `checkpoint_id` -> semantically admitted Checkpoint Record (`Reader.CheckpointRecords` through the shared owner: owning lease tuple in winning ancestry, creator-holder, Session.kind variant, head closure via the shared helpers; chain + kind threaded from `winningLeaseFor`) -> transitive closure over the winning-source index -> newest change. Source resolved against the REFERENCED closure. Missing/wrong-session/wrong-lease/wrong-creator/wrong-variant/unresolvable-head references refuse `observation_unavailable`; contradictory pairs refuse `integrity_failure`. Tests: ported `TestReview9ResumeReferencedCheckpoint`, `TestRev10ResumeReferencedCheckpoint` (10 modes x direct/task_board x winner/ancestor with class pins), `TestRev10ResumeOldPlanSubstitution` (integrity), `TestRev10ResumeReferencedWithdrawal` (unavailable), ported `TestReview10ReferencedCheckpointAdmission` (12 negatives + 4 controls, direct/task_board x winner/ancestor), `TestRev11ReferencedCheckpointAdmissionRefusalClass` (12 unavailable pins), `TestRev11ReferencedCheckpointAdmissionOldPlan` (12 old-plan unavailable), `TestRev11RecordConsumptionCensus` (call-graph gate), updated `TestRev8ProfileResumePositiveControl` + `dangling_resume_source`. Plants: `N-profile-resume-missing` (admission kill), `N-profile-resume-newest` (admission kill), `N-referenced-creator/variant/lease` (each admits exactly one invalid referenced member; census tokens preserved, behavioral admission kills).\\\"\\n)\\nrev11 = head + \\\"| C6b-R5 |\\\" + r5_new + \\\"| C6b-R6 |\\\" + rest\\n# Update unguarded audit to mention rev11\\nold_audit = \\\"\\\"\\\"Every owned relationship above ships a production-entry regression.\\nCR9 P1-A (fork new-session pair) and P1-B (resume referenced-closure\\npair) were unguarded: a corrupt fork pair kept canonical identity,\\nsession, lease, epoch, creator, variant, and head resolution green\\nand was admitted by all four entries, and a resume citing a change\\noutside its referenced closure was admitted from the outer-walk\\nprefix. Both are repaired by this rework with the six-row census as\\nthe class-closing instrument: every (event kind x relationship) pair\\nin the pinned 5.2 sentence is either driven (R1-R6, all six) or\\ndeclared a caller bound with its owning clause named (provenance,\\nstorage existence, launch-mode, confirmation, CLI). No owned\\nrelationship is declared delegated: C5 names the canonical\\npublication gate that already carries its inputs; P1-caller names\\n`BoundariesFor`; C6a names `checkCheckpointEventHeads`;\\nC6b-R1..R6 name `checkClosureProfilePairs` with its winning-source\\nrecord/event/closure inputs plus, for R5, the already-supplied\\nadmitted Checkpoint Records threaded from the reader (no new store\\nwas introduced: `checkWinnerCheckpoint` and `checkCheckpointBinding`\\nalready held the validated map). The fork null-source pin that no\\nchained fixture can violate names the canonical append owner with\\nits observed refusal; the launch post-head citation bound names\\ncausal necessity with the historical admission control. The C6b\\nout-of-scope notes above cite the normative sentences that place\\neach item outside closure admission; none of them names a future API\\nas an authority owner.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nnew_audit = \\\"\\\"\\\"Every owned relationship above ships a production-entry regression.\\nCR9 P1-A (fork new-session pair) and P1-B (resume referenced-closure\\npair) were unguarded: a corrupt fork pair kept canonical identity,\\nsession, lease, epoch, creator, variant, and head resolution green\\nand was admitted by all four entries, and a resume citing a change\\noutside its referenced closure was admitted from the outer-walk\\nprefix. Both were repaired in rev10 with the six-row census as the\\nclass-closing instrument. CR10 P1 (fifth C6 member, referenced\\nCheckpoint Record consumed as authority after only session equality\\nand head membership) was unguarded in rev10: 12 of 12\\nwrong-creator/variant/lease negatives admitted through all four\\nentries. It is repaired in rev11 by routing the referenced record\\nthrough the shared semantic owner with the winning ancestry and\\nSession.kind it needs, with the K1-K7 record-consumption table as the\\nclass-closing instrument: every record the shared owner consumes\\n(Session Record, winner checkpoint, necessary-ancestor checkpoint,\\nREFERENCED resume checkpoint, lease records, profile.changed and\\nother events) names its admission owner, call site, positive control,\\nnegatives, and narrowing plant; 7 of 7 rows driven, 0 undriven. No\\nowned relationship is declared delegated: C5 names the canonical\\npublication gate that already carries its inputs; P1-caller names\\n`BoundariesFor`; C6a names `checkCheckpointEventHeads`;\\nC6b-R1..R6 name `checkClosureProfilePairs` with its winning-source\\nrecord/event/closure inputs plus, for R5, the already-supplied\\nadmitted Checkpoint Records and winning ancestry threaded from the\\nreader (no new store, transport, publication, or materialization was\\nintroduced). The call-graph gate `TestRev11RecordConsumptionCensus`\\nfails if any K4 derivation reaches `profileClosure` without calling\\n`checkReferencedCheckpointBinding` first, and the three N-referenced\\ntoken-preserving plants prove the gate alone never suffices.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nassert old_audit in rev11\\nrev11 = rev11.replace(old_audit, new_audit)\\nout = pathlib.Path('.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_conformance-matrix-rev11.md')\\nout.write_text(rev11)\\nprint(f\\\"wrote {out} {len(rev11)} bytes\\\")\\nPY\\npython3 /tmp/gen_matrix_rev11.py\",\n  \"description\": \"Generate conformance matrix rev11\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"wrote .temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_conformance-matrix-rev11.md 22756 bytes\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 90,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 23,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
