{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e241","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0abc2-42f2-7250-afbe-0f50f97f1bdf"},"sequence":3963,"recorded_at":1780531400007921,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e1f5c30b-1aa7-4c3a-b177-a44d7d5421ad"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0abfb-ee8d-7e22-819d-4e82930adbe8"},"task_id":"01a0abfb-ee8d-7e22-819d-4e82930adbe8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0abfb-ee8d-7e22-819d-4e82930adbe8","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-16\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev10 rework: fork/resume profile authority closed by relation census\n9|- DEFECT (third verdict in the canonical-identity family, C6): the\n10|  shared profile gate derived every pair from the outer-walk prefix.\n11|  A fork.created event was never compared (no `fork.created` case),\n12|  so a corrupt new-session pair was admitted by all four entries\n13|  (CR9 P1-A, ported `TestReview9ForkLocalProfile` red baseline in\n14|  `.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/rev10-baseline-red.log`); a\n15|  session.resumed event ignored its `checkpoint_id`, so a pair from\n16|  outside its referenced closure was admitted (CR9 P1-B, ported\n17|  `TestReview9ResumeReferencedCheckpoint` red baseline in the same\n18|  log: 3 positives passed, 3 negatives admitted pre-fix).\n19|- FIX (`internal/sessquery/lease.go`, shared owner only): new\n20|  `fork.created` arm compares the event pair to the new Session\n21|  Record creation profile with a null source (`source_profile_event_id`\n22|  provenance never read); the `session.resumed` arm now derives its\n23|  expectation from its referenced checkpoint's own event-head closure\n24|  via `referencedCheckpointProfile` (admitted Checkpoint Records\n25|  threaded from the reader; no new store). Missing/wrong-session/\n26|  unresolvable references refuse observation_unavailable;\n27|  contradictory pairs refuse integrity_failure. Later-launch\n28|  derivation is unchanged by normative text (launches carry no\n29|  `checkpoint_id`) and is pinned by retained positives plus new\n30|  task_board.launched rows.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
